# Copy this file to `.env.local` (gitignored) and fill in the real value.
#
# Google requires a client_secret on the OAuth token exchange even for "Desktop app"
# clients using PKCE. It is not a true secret in that context (it ships inside the
# installed app), but keep it out of version control anyway: this repo is PUBLIC, and
# GitHub secret scanning reports committed Google client secrets — after which Google
# revokes them automatically and every installed copy stops being able to sign in.
#
# What actually limits who can use the extractable client ID/secret is the OAuth consent
# screen staying in Testing mode with an explicit test-user allowlist. Do not publish it.
#
# Find it at: Google Cloud Console -> APIs & Services -> Credentials
#             -> your OAuth 2.0 Client ID -> Client secret
MAIN_VITE_GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=
